  "strDescriptionEN": "Aar\u00f3n Ochoa Moloney (born 18 April 2007) is a footballer who plays as an attacking midfielder for Spanish club M\u00e1laga CF. Born in Spain, he is a Republic of Ireland youth international.\r\n\r\nBorn in Marbella, M\u00e1laga, Andalusia to an Irish mother and a Spanish father from La Rioja, Ochoa joined M\u00e1laga CF's youth setup at the age of nine, from CD Pe\u00f1a Los Compadres. He made his senior debut with the reserves on 22 October 2023, coming on as a second-half substitute in a 2\u20131 Tercera Federaci\u00f3n home loss to Juventud de Torremolinos CF.\r\n\r\nOchoa made his made his first team debut on 6 December 2023, replacing injured Juan Hern\u00e1ndez in the first half of a 1\u20130 home win over CD Eldense, for the season's Copa del Rey; aged 16 years, seven months and 18 days, he became the second-youngest player to debut for the club, only behind Fabrice Olinga. He scored his first senior goal the following 25 February, netting the B's opener in a 5\u20130 home routing of CD Torreperogil, and renewed his contract until 2027 on 17 April 2024.\r\n\r\nOchoa featured in nine matches with the main squad overall during the campaign, as the Blanquiazules achieved promotion to Segunda Divisi\u00f3n. He made his professional debut on 17 August 2024, starting in a 2\u20132 away draw against Racing de Ferrol.",
